## 4. Slice summary

The load-bearing HE3→HE6→HE7 and reconciliation mechanisms are genuinely characteristic-free: residue calculations occur over abstract finite fields; value calculations use discrete valuation, Newton polygons, resultants, and integer normalizer arithmetic; recursive termination uses completeness. The notes explicitly remove the bad ramified-base-change argument, fence every factor-orbit argument by `disc f ≠ 0`, and handle vanishing binomial coefficients in equal characteristic. I found one equal-characteristic-sensitive textual defect: HE3’s assertion that an irreducible key has a “full conjugate set.” Replacing that phrase with the determinant-norm/resultant formulation and counting geometric roots with multiplicity repairs it without new mathematics. The slice therefore supports by-finite-level generality across complete DVRs, including \(F_q[[t]]\), subject to the named out-of-slice interfaces—most notably the explicitly unsettled GENHN \(f_1\ge2\) count rerun.

